Aiuta Community License, version 1.0 — DRAFT

*** This is a draft written to describe the project owner's intent. It has
*** not been reviewed by a lawyer. Do not rely on it until it has been.

Copyright (c) 2026 Harry Catanzariti ("the Licensor")

1. What you may do for free

   Anyone may use, copy, change and share this software at no cost, for
   themselves, their family, their friends, or people they care for, and
   any non-profit, charity, community group, library, school, care home or
   health service may do the same for the people they serve, as long as
   they do not charge for it.

2. Hosting or selling it ("Commercial Use")

   "Commercial Use" means offering this software, or anything built from
   it, to other people in exchange for money or other payment, including:
   running it as a hosted or managed service, selling subscriptions,
   installation, devices or support bundled with it, or charging for its
   AI features.

   Commercial Use is allowed only if you:

   a. pay the Licensor ten percent (10%) of the gross revenue you receive
      from that Commercial Use, every three months, with a short written
      statement of how it was worked out; and
   b. tell the Licensor in writing before you start (contact details are in
      README.md).

   Charging only to pass on your actual costs (for example the AI provider's
   fees, at no markup) is still Commercial Use, but the 10% is owed only on
   the amount above those costs.

3. Changes go back to the project

   If you change this software and then share it, host it, or make it
   available to anyone outside your own household, you must:

   a. publish the source code of your changes under this same license; and
   b. offer them to the official repository
      (https://github.com/harrycatanzariti-oss/Auita) as a pull request.

   The Licensor is not obliged to accept a pull request.

4. Contributions

   By sending a contribution to the official repository you agree to the
   terms in CONTRIBUTING.md, including that the Licensor may use your
   contribution under this license or any other license.

5. Keep this notice

   Every copy, and anything built from it, must include this license and
   the copyright notice above.

6. No warranty

   The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. The
   Licensor is not liable for any damage or loss arising from its use. It is
   a convenience for opening programs and websites; it is not a medical,
   emergency or safety device.

7. Ending the license

   If you break these terms, your permission ends automatically. It comes
   back if you fix the breach (including paying anything owed) within 30
   days of being told about it.
